  "obligation": "Execute ref.cast_desc_eq and both descriptor branch-casts through the single VM, preserving descriptor identity, exactness, null-trap precedence and original branch references/payloads.",
  "representation": "ReferenceTarget derives descriptor input types from the original declaration graph and target exactness. One wasm_descriptor_matches operation validates the descriptor, traps on null before examining the source, admits null sources only for nullable targets and compares the original stored descriptor identity for live GC objects. Two appended residual operations share that predicate: cast returns the original reference or a descriptor-cast trap; test supplies the existing structured branch operation, with the failure form inverting its condition. Existing reference branch lowering owns both branch and fallthrough moves. Module registration requires the target descriptor relationship before effects. Format69 admits the appended operations without changing packed widths; no cell, side map, allocation or executor is added.",
